Hi,

looking at the "Weblinks" page, found some dead links:
- RT Firewire currently points to an error page:
http://rtfirewire.dynamized.com/
- Ethercat master library points to a page saying that the project is
discontinued:
http://ethercatmaster.berlios.de/
- RTAI points to a page which has not been updated since 2010 (just kidding)
- the "Linux Live-CD Download" in the SCALE-RT section does not in fact
allow to download any CD, at least not immediately.

Some stuff on many pages is pretty much outdated (for instance, the
"bleeding edge stuff" in the "add-on repository" dates from 2007), but I
guess there is not much we can do about it. Except maybe removing the
weblinks page altogether. I mean, by looking around in the server logs,
I found many more pages talking about xenomai, so, I wonder if it really
makes sense to give links to pages currently outdated, and not giving
links to page with more recent material.

